  "x-scope": "B-L123-analyze_genomic_region_overlap::local",
  "x-external-record-resource": {
    "uri": "urn:gene-annotation:planning:genomic-overlap-contract-418:v1",
    "path": "../tool_graders_genomic_overlap_contract_2026-10-27_418/DATA_CONTRACT.json",
    "sha256": "feb53c29f02ac3c1663c998e37bc6cd399a28179a055af39a4175aab66f44b66"
  },
  "x-field-policy": "All fields required, object fields closed, null explicit; strict Python integers exclude booleans and numeric values must be finite. Semantic relationships in CONTRACT.md are mandatory and not implied by JSON Schema.",
  "x-semantic-validation": [
    "Request and every G1 record retain exact packet418/422 semantics and the later root metadata clarifications. No external artifact or workflow authority is granted by a record.",
    "Inputs match request set order/key exactly; paths are explicit authorized original sources; all unordered comparisons are frozen and complete.",
    "Outputs equal genomic_overlap_output_files(request) exactly; no caller-added path or role. Count = 5 + 4*n + 3*n*(n-1)/2.",
    "RequestedJob argv/environment equals compile_genomic_overlap_job(native_genomic_overlap) with nominal plan path. Realized command changes only the final token to absolute original plan pathname.",
    "Native allocation and every constraint equal the declared policy; derived action path, hashes and original assignment are exact.",
    "All large-byte staging, hashing, parsing, sorting, native calls and result calculations run in the selected bounded worker, never unbounded host catalog construction.",
    "Batch files equal Outputs except its own batch_manifest entry in original order; declaration path/format match specification and paths are unique.",
    "Every set and pair has exactly one output entry in original request order; manifest comparison endpoints and native identity are exact. Pair NativeDriverManifest is unchanged and contains no artifact_ref anywhere.",
    "Software version probe is one finite declared call iff a valid nonempty pair needs bedtools; actual observed fields are not filled when the driver or probe never ran.",
    "Pair manifest input_fingerprints are measured original bytes in A/B order, equal to selected request source identities. Missing/unverified source implies null pair manifest, not invented fingerprints.",
    "Executed pair files have canonical_a, canonical_b, overlap_stdout, overlap_stderr exactly in that order and declarations equal the batch entries reached through declared set/comparison relationships.",
    "Analytic empty manifest outcome is not_executed, with null invocation facts and no files; both sets must be complete and at least one empty. Batch disposition analytic_empty can satisfy mechanical completion without pretending a native call occurred.",
    "Malformed verified inputs use invalid_input/not_executed_invalid_input. Missing/mismatched source uses input_unavailable with null pair manifest. Unavailable binary/spawn uses native_unavailable with null pair manifest.",
    "A native dependency failure is converted by the result host to derivation bedtools_intersect + outcome not_executed + all invocation facts null/empty + unavailable extents, never invalid-input or supplied-output semantics.",
    "Sealing occurs after closure, independently per pair and finally per batch. Process interruption cannot be represented by an invented sealed batch.",
    "The same original action can reopen its handle or replay retained receipts but never rerun driver pairs; any new retry is a distinct selected action outside G2.",
    "DriverFailure indices resolve to actual same batch failure rows with matching applicable set/comparison. Input parse details are G1 Failure records in unchanged ParsedRegionSet files.",
    "Capture joins use original declaration order and exact role/path identity. Host Store artifact refs come only from actual capture or exact previously supplied original identities.",
    "Batch complete requires all input sets complete and all pairs native_succeeded or analytic_empty; parser completeness and reference identity remain separately qualified. CLI chosen exit 0/1 is verified against actual outer lifecycle returncode."
  ],
